  "summary_en": "Philosophical paper critiquing proposals (Gunkel, Coeckelbergh, Danaher) that robot rights should be considered now. It rejects the relational turn, ethical behaviourism and denial of the is/ought distinction, suggests empathy yields a \"derived moral status\", and concludes robot rights are not a current issue.",
